an>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:29:00-07:00","id":855407,"title":"","content":"I would just throw on &quot;What We Do in the Shadows&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T18:34:35-07:00","id":855412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855301-world-of-dorkness-how-would-you-parody-your-favorite-game?p=855407#post855407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just throw on &quot;What We Do in the Shadows&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I forgot about that one! <br /> Now I have to write the Procession of Shame as an Ignoblis Ritae. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T05:38:06-07:00","id":855636,"title":"","content":"I sort of did once - I made a convention scenario called &quot;Dracula Must Die!&quot; for the Feng Shui RPG, which was all about cramming as many overwrought &quot;silver-katanas-and-black-leather-trenchcoats&quot; Vampire tropes into one game night as I possibly could. The premade PCs were an Abomination named after Samuel Haight, Dracula's redemption-seeking &quot;daughter&quot;, a crazy badass human vampire hunter and an eerie little kid who was actually a Tremere Elder.<br /> <br /> Besides some investigation and connective scenes, the scenario included a fight against an army of vampire ninjas in a Hong Kong penthouse, firebombing Castle Dracula and digging through the catacombs underneath when it became clear Dracula had somehow survived, and an awful set-piece battle against Dracula's monstrous flesh-and-blood underground lair modelled on the Cathedral of Flesh, which the PCs had to cut their way through before Dracula, who formed its &quot;heart&quot;, went full Akira and effectively hijacked Gehenna to become the new God-King of vampires (and the world).<br /> <br /> Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:52:17-07:00","id":856078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Schleiermacher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/855301-world-of-dorkness-how-would-you-parody-your-favorite-game?p=855636#post855636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sort of did once - I made a convention scenario called &quot;Dracula Must Die!&quot; for the Feng Shui RPG, which was all about cramming as many overwrought &quot;silver-katanas-and-black-leather-trenchcoats&quot; Vampire tropes into one game night as I possibly could. The premade PCs were an Abomination named after Samuel Haight, Dracula's redemption-seeking &quot;daughter&quot;, a crazy badass human vampire hunter and an eerie little kid who was actually a Tremere Elder.<br /> <br /> Besides some investigation and connective scenes, the scenario included a fight against an army of vampire ninjas in a Hong Kong penthouse, firebombing Castle Dracula and digging through the catacombs underneath when it became clear Dracula had somehow survived, and an awful set-piece battle against Dracula's monstrous flesh-and-blood underground lair modelled on the Cathedral of Flesh, which the PCs had to cut their way through before Dracula, who formed its &quot;heart&quot;, went full Akira and effectively hijacked Gehenna to become the new God-King of vampires (and the world).<br /> <br /> Good times.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the most awesome and bad ass thing i have ever hear in a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:22:30-07:00","id":856097,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Legend_of_the_7_Golden_Vampires\" target=\"_blank\">I'll just put this out here...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T17:49:32-07:00","id":856107,"title":"","content":"I think someone already did... and called it Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Dat